-- ===== 5) 听力 6篇/30题(audio_url 待 TTS) =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_listening_exercises WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective2' AND unit='U2';
Tom: I''m thinking about Spanish. So many people around the world speak it.
Lily: That''s a good reason. What made you interested in the first place?
Tom: Last month I watched a Spanish film and loved how the language sounded.
Lily: I know what you mean. I want to learn Japanese myself.
Tom: Japanese? Why is that?
Lily: I love Japanese stories, and I''d like to read them in the original language.
Tom: That''s great. Learning any new language opens a door to another world.', 'Lily 问 Tom 明年选哪门外语;Tom 想学西班牙语,因为说的人多;他上个月看了部西班牙电影,喜欢那语言的声音;Lily 想学日语,因为喜欢日本故事,想读原文;Tom 说学任何新语言都会打开通往另一个世界的门。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which language is Tom thinking of taking?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Spanish.","Japanese.","French.","Russian."]},{"q":"Why did Tom become interested in that language?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["His teacher chose it for him.","He watched a film and loved how it sounded.","It is the easiest one to spell.","Almost no one else speaks it."]},{"q":"Which language does Lily want to learn?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Japanese.","Spanish.","Arabic.","German."]},{"q":"Why does Lily want to learn it?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She no longer likes English.","She wants to read Japanese stories in the original.","She is moving abroad next week.","Her parents made her choose it."]},{"q":"What does Tom say about learning a new language?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is mostly a waste of time.","It can harm the brain.","It opens a door to another world.","It is only useful for exams."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Today only a small number of them are still used every day.
Europeans arrived a little over two hundred years ago, and many languages slowly died out.
For Aboriginal communities, language is a central part of who they are.
It links them to their land, their history, and their sense of belonging.', '很久以前,澳大利亚有数百种不同的语言;如今只有少数仍在日常使用;欧洲人两百多年前到来,许多语言渐渐消亡;对原住民社区来说,语言是他们身份的核心;它把他们与土地、历史和归属感相连。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"About how many languages were once spoken in Australia?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only two.","About seven.","None at all.","Hundreds."]},{"q":"How many of them are still used daily now?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Only a small number.","Almost all of them.","Exactly one hundred.","More than before."]},{"q":"When did Europeans arrive, according to the talk?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only last year.","A little over two hundred years ago.","Five thousand years ago.","They never arrived."]},{"q":"What is language for Aboriginal communities?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A brand-new invention.","An unimportant daily habit.","A central part of their identity.","A foreign import they dislike."]},{"q":"What does their language link them to?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only their money.","Only the weather.","Nothing in particular.","Their land, history, and sense of belonging."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Igor: Different, of course. One is light blue and the other is dark blue.
Anna: Really? To me they both look just ''blue''.
Igor: In Russian we have two separate words, so I notice the line between them at once.
Anna: That''s amazing. So your language trains your eyes a little.
Igor: Maybe. Scientists say Russian speakers are faster at telling these blues apart.
Anna: I''d never have guessed that words could change how quickly we see.
Igor: It shows how deeply language and the mind are connected.', 'Anna 让 Igor 看两个方块是否同色;Igor 说不同,一个浅蓝一个深蓝;Anna 觉得两个都只是''蓝'';Igor 说俄语里有两个分开的词,所以一眼就看出界线;Anna 惊叹语言训练了眼睛;Igor 说研究表明俄语者更快区分这些蓝色;两人感叹语言与思维联系之深。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How do the two squares look to Anna?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They both look simply ''blue''.","They look like two different reds.","They look completely black.","She cannot see them at all."]},{"q":"Why does Igor notice the difference at once?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["He is wearing special glasses.","Russian has two separate words for the blues.","He painted the squares himself.","English has far more colour words."]},{"q":"What do scientists say about Russian speakers?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They cannot see the colour blue.","They are always much slower.","They tell these blues apart faster.","They ignore colours completely."]},{"q":"What surprises Anna about words?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["That words have no meaning at all.","That blue is her favourite colour.","That Russian is very easy to learn.","That words can change how quickly we see."]},{"q":"What does the talk show, according to Igor?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Language and the mind are deeply connected.","Colours do not really exist.","Russian is a useless language.","Our eyes never change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Every time you switch between them, your brain gets a small workout.
Studies show that this effort can keep the mind sharp for longer.
It may even delay certain memory problems by several years.
So learning a language is not only useful; it is good for the brain.', '会说两种语言不只是能和更多人交流;每次在两种语言间切换,大脑都会做个小锻炼;研究表明这种努力能让头脑更久保持敏锐;甚至可能把某些记忆问题推迟数年;所以学语言不仅有用,还有益大脑。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What happens each time you switch languages?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Your brain stops working.","Your brain gets a small workout.","You forget your first language.","Nothing at all changes."]},{"q":"What do the studies show?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Two languages harm the mind.","Switching is simply impossible.","The effort can keep the mind sharp for longer.","Memory gets worse straight away."]},{"q":"What may speaking two languages delay?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Learning how to read.","Growing any taller.","Making new friends.","Certain memory problems."]},{"q":"How long might it delay them?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By several years.","By a few minutes.","By a single day.","Not at all."]},{"q":"What is the speaker''s main point?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Languages are a waste of time.","A language is useful and good for the brain.","Only one language is ever needed.","The brain never changes."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');
Sam: That''s a pity. What happens when the last speakers are gone?
Mei: A lot of stories and local knowledge could disappear with them.
Sam: So have you thought of doing anything about it?
Mei: Yes. Every weekend I record him telling old tales in his dialect.
Sam: That''s a wonderful idea. You''re saving more than just words.
Mei: Exactly. The real question is whether my generation will keep it alive.
Sam: I''m sure small efforts like yours can make a real difference.', 'Mei 说爷爷讲一种几乎没年轻人用的老方言;Sam 觉得可惜,问最后的说话者走后会怎样;Mei 说许多故事和地方知识可能随之消失;Mei 每个周末录爷爷用方言讲老故事;Sam 称赞这是在拯救不止是词语的东西;Mei 说真正的问题是她这代人能否让它存续;Sam 相信小小的努力能带来真正的改变。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is special about Mei''s grandpa''s dialect?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Everyone in the city speaks it.","It is a brand-new language.","Few young people still use it.","It is taught in every school."]},{"q":"What could disappear with the last speakers?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only the spelling rules.","Nothing of any value.","A few old road signs.","Stories and local knowledge."]},{"q":"What does Mei do every weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She records him telling old tales.","She forgets the dialect on purpose.","She studies only English.","She travels far abroad."]},{"q":"What does Sam say she is really saving?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only a little money.","More than just words.","A pile of old books.","Nothing important at all."]},{"q":"What does Mei call the real question?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Where her grandpa now lives.","How old the dialect really is.","Whether her generation will keep it alive.","Why English is so useful."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');
But this talk is not really about how people far away think.
It is about how you, yourself, think every single day.
Your language quietly shapes what you notice and what you forget.
So it is always worth asking why you see the world the way you do.', '我们看到说不同语言的人可能以不同方式思考;但这次演讲并非真的关于远方的人如何思考;而是关于你自己每天如何思考;你的语言悄悄塑造你注意什么、忽略什么;所以值得问问:你为何这样看世界。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What have we seen about speakers of different languages?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They all think exactly the same.","They are unable to think.","They never use any words.","They can think in different ways."]},{"q":"What is this talk really about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["How you yourself think.","How people far away think.","How to spell English words.","How to travel abroad cheaply."]},{"q":"What does your language quietly shape?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only how tall you grow.","What you notice and what you forget.","Only the weather outside.","Nothing about your mind."]},{"q":"How often does language shape your thinking?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only once a year.","Never in real life.","Every single day.","Only during exams."]},{"q":"What does the speaker say is worth asking?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Where you were first born.","How tall your friends are.","Who your teacher is.","Why you see the world as you do."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='sufe' AND volume='elective2' AND unit='U2';

I am writing to ask the school to offer a French course. I strongly believe that high school students should be able to learn a language other than English.

It is true that English is already used in business, science and travel around the world. However, this does not mean that one language is enough. What a new language really offers is a fresh way of seeing the world and a chance to reach millions more people. The truth is that every language we learn quietly changes how we think.

Many of my classmates feel the same way. I would be grateful if the school could consider opening a French class.

Yours sincerely,
Chen Kai', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["I strongly believe that high school students should be able to learn a language other than English.","It is true that English is widely used; however, this does not mean that one language is enough.","What a new language really offers is a fresh way of seeing the world.","The truth is that every language we learn quietly changes how we think."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"I believe that students should to learn French.","correct":"I believe that students should learn French.","note":"情态动词 should 后接动词原形,不加 to。"},{"wrong":"The truth is what every language changes our thinking.","correct":"The truth is that every language changes our thinking.","note":"表语从句陈述事实、从句完整,用 that 不用 what。"},{"wrong":"What a new language offers are a new way of thinking.","correct":"What a new language offers is a new way of thinking.","note":"What 引导的主语从句作主语视为单数,谓语用 is。"}]'::jsonb, '【劝说信结构】
开头 说明目的 + 主张:I am writing to … I strongly believe that …
中间 反方+反驳:It is true that … However, this does not mean that …
中间 理由:What a new language offers is … The truth is that …
结尾 请求:I would be grateful if the school could …', 2, 'elective2', 'U2', 'sufe');

